Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:18:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] engine: a save in three steps (prepare, run, finish)

file.save took the snapshot, serialized it, wrote the file and recorded the result in one call on the caller's thread. The steps are now separate: Session::prepare_save takes the path, the format and the workbook as it is (an immutable snapshot), SaveJob::run serializes and writes without a session, on any thread, and Session::finish_save records the result in its document by uid. file.save runs the three in a row, with the same bytes and the same document state as before. When the document was edited between the first and the last step, the file holds the snapshot, the edits stay and the document stays unsaved; its saved state is the snapshot, so undoing back to it makes it clean. A PDF and a workbook without a file are not prepared (file.save handles them). Session::save_can_be_detached says when the steps may be spread over frames: not while actions are recorded, a macro is debugged or an undo group is open.

Tests: save_job (10); the engine suite passes unchanged.
